---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

/**
 * The keystone document. Grounded in docs/website-recon/RAW-legal.json.
 *
 * Three things in here are deliberate and must not be "cleaned up":
 *
 * 1. The messaging provider is disclosed as a CATEGORY ("messaging
 *    infrastructure providers, EU-hosted"), never by vendor name. GDPR
 *    Art 13(1)(e) permits "categories of recipients". What is NOT permitted —
 *    and what would be an affirmative false statement under FTC Act §5 — is
 *    implying WhatsApp data reaches only Meta. It does not, and this document
 *    never says it does.
 *
 * 2. German processing is stated plainly. The company is American; the servers
 *    are not. Concealing that mismatch is what turns it into a §5 problem.
 *
 * 3. Facts that do not exist yet (EU/UK representatives, the CNDP filing) are
 *    marked in-progress rather than asserted. A policy claiming a filing that
 *    hasn't happened is the exact failure this whole exercise exists to avoid.
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How iGrowFast LLC collects, uses, stores and shares personal data — including what we hold for our own users and what we process on behalf of the businesses that use us."
  path="/privacy"
  updated="16 July 2026"
  summary="What we do with personal data — ours, our customers', and their customers'. Written to be read, not to be survived."
>
  <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This service is operated by <strong>iGrowFast LLC</strong>, a limited
    liability company formed in Wyoming, United States.
  </p>
  <address>
    iGrowFast LLC<br />
    30 N Gould St Ste R<br />
    Sheridan, WY 82801<br />
    United States<br />
    <a href="mailto:privacy@igrowfast.com">privacy@igrowfast.com</a>
  </address>
  <p>
    <strong>Where your data actually is.</strong> We are an American company,
    but our servers are not in America. The platform runs on infrastructure
    located in <strong>Germany</strong>, and backups and stored files are held
    in the <strong>European Union</strong>. We state this here, at the top,
    because it is the sort of thing a privacy policy should not bury.
  </p>

  <h2 id="roles">2. Two different roles — this matters for your rights</h2>
  <p>
    iGrowFast is software used by businesses to run their own operations. That
    means we handle two very different kinds of personal data, and our
    responsibility is different for each.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Whose data</th><th>Our role</th><th>What that means for you</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Our own users — the people who log in to iGrowFast (business owners, sellers, media buyers, couriers)</td>
          <td><strong>Controller</strong></td>
          <td>We decide what we collect and why. Bring your requests directly to us.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>End customers — people who bought something from a business that uses iGrowFast (name, phone, delivery address, order contents, chat messages)</td>
          <td><strong>Processor</strong></td>
          <td>The business you bought from decides what happens to your data. We only act on their instructions. See <a href="/data-deletion">Your Privacy Rights &amp; Data Deletion</a> — we will route you to them.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    If you are an end customer and you contact us, we will not quietly ignore
    you — but we generally cannot delete or change your data on our own
    authority, because it isn't ours. We will identify the business that holds
    it and pass your request on.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what">3. What we collect</h2>
  <h3>From our users</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Account details: name, username, email address, phone number, role, and which business you belong to.</li>
    <li>Authentication data: a hashed password, session records, and — if you enable it — two-factor authentication settings.</li>
    <li>Usage and security records: sign-in events, IP address and approximate location derived from it, and browser/device information.</li>
    <li>Anything you type into the product.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>On behalf of our customers (their end customers' data)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Order data: names, phone numbers, delivery addresses, cities and zones, order contents and prices, delivery and return status.</li>
    <li>Message content: the text, images, audio, documents and metadata of conversations conducted through the business's own messaging numbers.</li>
    <li>Contact records the business imports or creates.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>From visitors to this website</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Standard server and security logs.</li>
    <li>Cookies and similar technologies — but only the strictly necessary ones unless you consent. See our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="why">4. Why we use it, and our legal basis</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (where the GDPR applies)</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Providing the product to the business you work for</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Keeping accounts secure; detecting abuse; sign-in alerts</td><td>Legitimate interests (security)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Verifying an email address at signup</td><td>Legitimate interests (preventing fraud and undeliverable accounts)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Analytics and advertising on this website</td><td><strong>Consent</strong> — nothing is set until you agree, and you can withdraw at any time</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Processing end-customer data inside the product</td><td>Determined by our customer, who is the controller. We act on their instructions.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Meeting legal and accounting obligations</td><td>Legal obligation</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="recipients">5. Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal data. We do not share it with data brokers. We use
    a small number of service providers, described here by category:
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Category</th><th>What they handle</th><th>Where</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Hosting and infrastructure</td><td>The application, the database, and everything in it</td><td>Germany</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Object storage and backups</td><td>Uploaded files, media, and encrypted backups</td><td>European Union</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Messaging infrastructure providers</td><td>Sending and receiving messages on your business's numbers, including message content and the phone numbers involved</td><td>European Union</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Email delivery</td><td>Transactional email we send you</td><td>European Union</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Email verification</td><td>Checking an address is deliverable at signup</td><td>European Union / United States</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Bot and abuse protection</td><td>Challenge checks on sign-in forms</td><td>Global edge network</td></tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Analytics and advertising <span class="wip">Not yet active</span></td>
          <td>Website measurement and ad measurement — <strong>only if you consent</strong></td>
          <td>United States / global</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>AI providers <span class="wip">Not yet in production</span></td>
          <td>Not currently used in the product</td>
          <td>United States</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    We describe these by category rather than by brand because the specific
    vendors within a category change over time, and a list of names goes stale
    faster than it helps. If you are a customer and need the current named list
    for your own compliance records, ask us and we will provide it under our
    <a href="/dpa">Data Processing Addendum</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What we will not claim.</strong> Messages sent through the product
    are handled by the messaging infrastructure described above as well as by
    the messaging platform itself. We are not going to tell you your messages
    only ever touch one company, because that would not be true.
  </p>

  <h3>Advertising on this website</h3>
  <p>
    If you consent to marketing cookies, this website can load measurement tags
    from advertising platforms. For some of these — notably the Meta pixel —
    the platform and iGrowFast act as <strong>joint controllers</strong> for the
    collection and transmission of that data, following the Court of Justice's
    decision in <em>Fashion ID</em> (C-40/17). Consent is asked for before
    anything loads, and refusing is exactly as easy as accepting.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="wip">In progress</span> These tags are configured but not yet
    activated — no advertising or analytics identifiers are currently issued by
    this website. This section describes what happens when they are, and it will
    not change what we ask you for: consent first.
  </p>

  <h2 id="transfers">6. Sending data across borders</h2>
  <p>
    Personal data in the product is processed in Germany and stored in the
    European Union. Some data reaches the United States, because we are an
    American company and some of our providers are American.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where data leaves the European Economic Area, we rely on the European
    Commission's <strong>Standard Contractual Clauses</strong>, together with an
    assessment of the destination country's laws and additional safeguards
    where needed.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="wip">In progress</span> Our transfer documentation is being
    completed, including the authorisation required under Moroccan law for
    transfers abroad. See section 10.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">7. How long we keep it</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Kept for</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Account data for our users</td><td>While the account is active, then deleted or anonymised after closure</td></tr>
        <tr><td>End-customer and order data</td><td>For as long as our customer instructs. They decide; we act on it.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Message content</td><td>As above — set by the business operating the number</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Security and sign-in logs</td><td>A limited period, for security investigation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Backups</td><td>Rotated on a schedule; deletions propagate as backups age out</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    <span class="wip">In progress</span> We are publishing exact retention
    periods per data category. We would rather leave this marked than print a
    number our deletion jobs do not actually honour.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access your data,
    correct it, delete it, restrict or object to how it is used, receive a
    portable copy, and withdraw consent at any time. If you are in California,
    you also have rights to know, delete, correct, and to opt out of sale or
    sharing — <strong>we do not sell or share personal data</strong> as those
    terms are defined there.
  </p>
  <p>
    Start at <a href="/data-deletion">Your Privacy Rights &amp; Data Deletion</a>,
    or email <a href="mailto:privacy@igrowfast.com">privacy@igrowfast.com</a>.
    We respond within one month, and will tell you if we need longer.
  </p>
  <p>Exercising a right never costs you anything and never degrades your service.</p>

  <h2 id="representatives">9. Representatives in the EU and UK</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="wip">In progress</span> Where we are required to appoint a
    representative in the European Union (Article 27 GDPR) and in the United
    Kingdom, those appointments are being made and their details will be
    published here. We are not going to name a representative before one is
    actually appointed under a written mandate.
  </p>
  <p>
    Until then, contact us directly at
    <a href="mailto:privacy@igrowfast.com">privacy@igrowfast.com</a>. Your rights
    apply regardless, and we will honour them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="morocco">10. Morocco</h2>
  <p>
    Many of the businesses using iGrowFast operate in Morocco, and much of the
    personal data in the product belongs to people there. Moroccan law
    (Loi 09-08) requires processing to be declared to the
    <abbr title="Commission Nationale de contrôle de la protection des Données à caractère Personnel">CNDP</abbr>,
    and requires authorisation for transferring personal data abroad.
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class="wip">In progress</span> Our CNDP declaration and the transfer
    authorisations are being filed. The reference numbers will be published here
    and on <a href="/legal">Legal Notices</a> once issued.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">11. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Access is restricted by role, and enforced by the database itself rather
    than only by the interface. Traffic is encrypted in transit. Credentials and
    secrets are held in a dedicated secret store. Backups are encrypted.
    Administrative access to servers is key-based only.
  </p>
  <p>
    We are not going to tell you our systems cannot be breached. If a breach
    affects personal data, we will notify the relevant authority and affected
    people as the law requires.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">12. Children</h2>
  <p>
    iGrowFast is a business tool and is not directed at children. We do not
    knowingly collect data from anyone under 16. If you believe we have, tell us
    and we will remove it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">13. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Covered separately, in detail, in our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
    You can change your choices at any time using the “Cookie settings” link in
    the footer of every page.
  </p>

  <h2 id="complaints">14. Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    Tell us first — <a href="mailto:privacy@igrowfast.com">privacy@igrowfast.com</a>
    — and we will try to fix it. You also have the right to complain to a data
    protection authority: in the EU, the supervisory authority where you live or
    work; in the UK, the Information Commissioner's Office; in Morocco, the CNDP.
    You do not need our permission, and you do not need to contact us first.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">15. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy in a way that materially affects you, we will tell
    you rather than quietly reposting it. The date at the top always reflects the
    current version.
  </p>
</Legal>
